  "version": "draft-3",
  "updated": "2026-11-19",
  "about": "General gear progression rules the bot follows. Derived from the community chart (source-chart.webp) and our own decisions. Draft: not read by the bot yet.",
  "principles": [
    "Every slot has a ladder: base -> better pieces -> end goal. Each step has a target upgrade level.",
    "Keep upgrading instead of waiting: the worn piece goes up to its cap until the next step is in hand.",
    "The game's progression valuation decides what is better (the bot's equip pass already uses it). The plan only says what to wish for and what stands in.",
    "A missing item is replaced by its stand-in (e.g. green Lolipop Mace for the orange one).",
    "Wish: shop, craft and farmable drops are pursued actively. Found: event and boss items are worn when we have them, never chased.",
    "Team stages: jewelry goes up level by level for the whole team - the next level is wished only once every fighter wears the current one in all its slots; spare copies make the next step.",
    "A worn alternative pauses the ladder of its slot: while e.g. a Loaded Die is worn because it rates higher, no class orb is built.",
    "Shop weapons stop at +8 and only while no better copy is there (a worn Fiery Blade +7 already beats a Blade +8: 54 + burn vs 50). Above that the fire weapon ladder is the way up (Blade +9: 58, Fiery Blade +8: 60).",
    "Wanderer's set: each piece has the stats of the shop piece of its slot plus a little (cap +120 HP, attire +80 MP, breeches +1 speed) and the set bonus (2: +200 HP, 3: +100 MP, 4: +10% gold, 5: +16 luck). It replaces the shop piece at the same level and is upgraded instead of it. Not for tanks on the Rugged set."
  ],
